# sn0wbite T8006 adaptation of the qemu-t8030 fork. Apply: cd qemu-t8030 && git apply <this>; build;
# run with -smp 2. See docs/watchos/qemu-build-and-boot.md. Covers: A13 CPU node optional for
# Tempest(S5); sn0w CPU layer sn0w_cpu.{c,h}: RAZ/WI Apple IMPDEF(op0=3,CRn=15) + real R/W APRR_EL0/EL1
# (S3_4_C15_C2_0/1, CPUARMState.sprr.aprr_el[]) so the pmap PPL/xPRR check AND the PPL gate readback
# pass; a bring-up APRR MMU write-grant in ptw.c (EL1 RO non-exec pages -> R/W) so PPL can write its
# pages; GTIMER_PHYS wired to the CPU FIQ (apple_a13.c) -- watchOS uses the physical timer, the fork
# wired only the virtual one, so the timer FIQ was never delivered; minimal machine (coprocessors
# skipped, nvram optional, 4 GB DRAM kept -- do NOT shrink); DT timebase + load-time seed of
# gPEClockFrequencyInfo; KEEP_COMP += apple,tempest; tolerant no-op of the IODeviceTree interrupt
# resolver (now DISABLED, see below).
#
# Console (prior revision): model the Apple DockChannel UART -- the watchOS S5 serial console, not
# the Samsung uart0 (XNU 6153 pexpert dockchannel.h/pe_serial.c reg layout: WDATA1 TX +0x4004,
# WSTAT free-space +0x4014, RX regs empty). Its register windows sit INSIDE the broad pmgr
# placeholder range, so map them at priority 1 (add_subregion_overlap) to shadow it; DockChannel
# takes serial_hd(0), the Samsung UARTs shift to serial_hd(i+1); xnu.c KEEPS the dockchannel-uart
# DT node. Set /chosen debug-enabled = 1: a production-fused unit leaves it 0, which makes
# PE_i_can_has_debugger() false and SUPPRESSES the serial console + kprintf -- the gate that kept
# early boot silent.
#
# BREAKTHROUGH (prior revision): the fork's DT filter in xnu.c macho_dtb_node_process removes any
# node whose `compatible` is not in KEEP_COMP[] -- the list had `arm-io,s8000`/`arm-io,t8030` but
# NOT `arm-io,t8006`, so the ENTIRE /arm-io subtree (AIC, PMGR, DockChannel console node,
# coprocessors) was stripped from the kernel's DT -> gIODTPHandles empty -> IODeviceTree interrupt
# resolver NULL-dereffed on CPUs' interrupt-parent phandle 0x10 (AIC) -> no console, no interrupts.
# Fix: xnu.c KEEP_COMP += arm-io,t8006 + pmgr1,t8006 + gpio,t8006 + i2c,t8006 + wdt,t8006 +
# aic,t8006 + dockchannel,t8002 + dockchannel-uart + mcc,t8006 + error-handler,t8006. T8030_AIC:
# pad aic ipid-mask from 52->56 bytes (apple_aic_create rounds numEIR up to 14 ->
# AppleInterruptControllerV1.cpp:128 "length is 52 but should be 56"); AIC registers (_aicVersion=2
# _aicNumExtInts=0x1c0=448 _aicNumIPIs=4).
#
# Driver bring-up (prior revision): the IOKit interrupt resolver no-op is REMOVED -- with /arm-io
# kept and the AIC registered, real IODeviceTree interrupt resolution works. ApplePMGR::initDriver
# is bypassed by marking all 14 PMGR bridges optional (optional-bridge-mask=0x3fff).
# AppleStockholmControl (NFC) dropped via REM_NAMES. dockchannel-uart gets channel-number=0 so the
# IOKit AppleDockChannel kext doesn't panic "Invalid channel-number".
#
# THIS REVISION -- full driver stack up, kernel reaches "Waiting on IOMedia Partition ID=0x1":
#
# [1] arm-io unimplemented catch-all. The T8006 SoC exposes many peripherals we do not model
#     (GPIOIC, extra dockchannel register blocks, misc clock/power blocks, ...). Every unmodelled
#     register access took a synchronous external abort (ESR DFSC 0x10) and killed the driver.
#     Map one lowest-priority (-1000) unimplemented device over the entire arm-io window
#     (create_unimplemented_device("arm-io-unimpl", soc_base_pa, soc_size)) so unknown reads return
#     0, writes are ignored. Real device models at priority 0 shadow this catch-all for their exact
#     sub-ranges, so each future per-device model automatically overrides it with no change here.
#     This single change unblocked AppleT8006GPIOIC, MemCacheController tunables, PlatformErrorHandler,
#     AES, I2C, RTBuddy(RTP) and the keystore stack in one go.
#
# [2] ApplePMGR MTR perf-state registration (closed kext, DT-shaped assert). ApplePMGR-527.100.13
#     dispatches per-RegMap at 0xFFFFFFF00868AD70 (bounds-checks w1 < 0xA); only the w1 == 2 branch
#     registers the MTR aging/voltage/tvm sub-regions, which panic
#     (ApplePMGRMTRSensor.cpp:107/108/142 "perfStateNb / _perfStateRegionRegisters.nb > 0") because
#     the mtr_N DT props and backing region data are absent on this adapted DT. We cannot ret the
#     whole dispatcher (it serves the other RegMaps too) and ret-ing each sub-method is
#     whack-a-mole, so reroute ONLY the w1 == 2 case to the dispatcher's OWN "nothing registered"
#     exit (0x868AEAC: str xzr,[slot]; mov w0,#0; retab) -- same result it already returns for
#     empty/other-RegMap cases. Patch at 0x868ADC0: "b.ne 0x868AEAC" -> "b 0x868AEAC".
#
# [3] AppleDockChannel::start cleanly skipped. The IOKit AppleDockChannel kext (diags/rtp/bulk
#     channels, NOT the console path) maps six register blocks (global, dock-agent-AP, device
#     config/data, dock config/data); our QEMU dockchannel model only backs the UART sub-window used
#     by the low-level pexpert console. Its first MMIO read on an unmodelled block took an external
#     abort; make its start() return 0 ("mov w0,#0; ret" at 0xFFFFFFF00881529C) and IOKit detaches it
#     without touching the working console.
#
# [4] pmgr_reg[] OUT-OF-BOUNDS R/W fixed (real memory-safety bug in the fork). The T8006 pmgr
#     reg[0] window is 0x180000 bytes, but T8030MachineState.pmgr_reg was a FIXED uint8_t[0x100000].
#     The MemoryRegion was sized to reg[0] (0x180000), so pmgr_reg_read/write did
#     `memcpy(tms->pmgr_reg + addr, ...)` with NO bounds check, silently reading/writing
#     ADJACENT HOST STRUCT MEMORY for every guest access past 0x100000. ApplePMGR CPM's PS register
#     at 0x100040 therefore returned 0xf6404000 (next struct field), nibble 0 -> _setPSLevel panic
#     "MANUAL_PS=0 for CPM" (ApplePMGR.cpp:4421). Fixed by sizing pmgr_reg[] to 0x180000 and adding
#     a defence-in-depth bounds-check in the ops (returns 0 / drops on OOB).
#
# [5] -initrd -> rd=md0 wiring (ramdisk mountroot). In the pristine fork the "-restore rd=md0"
#     cmdline is only prepended when nvram.auto-boot==false, and our minimal machine skips the
#     nvram device entirely -- so the ramdisk was loaded (macho_load_ramdisk + DT RAMDisk prop set)
#     but the kernel never saw the rd= boot arg, falling back to "Waiting on IOMedia". Added a
#     parallel wiring in the no-nvram branch: when machine->initrd_filename is set, prepend
#     "rd=md0 " to the user cmdline. Omit -restore / -progress (they trigger restore-boot
#     validations + progress-UI hooks that panic silently on our machine); plain rd=md0 is enough
#     for XNU's BSD root path to create /dev/md0 from the loaded ramdisk and mount it.
#
# Boot status with this revision: full IOKit init runs to the end. corecrypto/FIPS PASSED ->
# CoreAnalyticsHub -> Image4 -> AppleT8006IO (B1) -> AppleInterruptController (AIC) ->
# AppleT8006GPIOIC -> AppleT8006MemCacheController + tunables -> AppleT8006PlatformErrorHandler
# (SEP_FUSE, AMCC/AMCX/CP/DT0/CCU0 maps) -> AppleS8000AES v3 -> AppleARMLightEmUp ->
# AppleS5L8940XI2CController i2c1/i2c3 -> RTBuddy(RTP) -> AppleKeyStore + AppleSEPKeyStore
# (_sep_enabled=1) -> AppleCredentialManager -> AppleSSE -> MemCacheController::start finished ->
# AppleMobileApNonce (timeout AES, expected, no HW) -> AppleARMPE::getGMTTimeOfDay (no RTC,
# expected) -> apfs_module_start v1412.100.68 -> AppleFSCompressionTypeZlib ->
# IOSurfaceRoot::installMemoryRegions() -> "Waiting on IOMedia Partition ID=0x1". The kernel is now

# idle waiting on the root block device. Passing the OTA's own ramdisk via -initrd (the IM4P-wrapped
# arm64_32SURamDisk.dmg from AssetData/payload/replace/usr/standalone/update/ramdisk/) now lands:
#   BSD root: md0, major 3, minor 0
#   apfs_vfsop_mount: unable to root from devvp (root_device): 2   (DMG is HFS+, not APFS)
#   hfs: mounted GraceUpdate17U224.arm64_32SURamDisk on device b(3, 0)
# -- the kernel mounts the Watch 6.3.1 Restore ramdisk as root. After that the console goes quiet,
# which is expected for a restore ramdisk: launchd takes over, routes further logs through ASL/syslog
# instead of kprintf, and com.apple.restored opens its XPC listener waiting for a paired iPhone that
# never arrives. Next milestones: confirm userland with -s (single-user shell on serial), then
# reconstruct the full rootfs from AssetData/payloadv2/ for SpringBoard/UI.

