+     * exit (0x868AEAC: str xzr,[slot]; mov w0,#0; retab) -- the same result it
+     * already returns for the empty/other-RegMap cases. Patch the branch at
+     * 0x868ADC0 "b.ne 0x868AEAC" (taken when w1 != 2) into an unconditional
+     * "b 0x868AEAC", so w1 == 2 takes it as well. No MTR telemetry is registered;
+     * the caller already tolerates the null/0 result.
+     * TODO: synthesise the mtr_N DT nodes + perf-state region data (closed-kext
+     * format) to register for real; until then this is the intended "skip extras"
+     * bring-up patch. */
+    *(uint32_t *)vtop_static(0xFFFFFFF00868ADC0) = 0x1400003b; /* b 0x868AEAC */
+
+    /* sn0w (bring-up, "skip extras"): AppleDockChannel::start (entry
+     * 0xFFFFFFF00881529C) maps and pokes six dockchannel register blocks (global,
+     * dock-agent-AP, device config/data, dock config/data). Our QEMU dockchannel
+     * model only backs the UART sub-window used by the low-level pexpert serial
+     * console (the path that prints this very log); the other blocks aren't decoded,
+     * so the driver's first MMIO read ([base+4] at 0x88156A4) takes an external
+     * abort (ESR DFSC 0x10), and it also rejects the node's channel-number. The
+     * IOKit AppleDockChannel kext (diags/rtp/bulk channels) is NOT the console path
